# .dockerignore - build-context filter for the multi-stage Dockerfile at the repository root.
#
# Intent (least-privilege, minimal-surface container): the SDK build stage restores, builds,
# tests, and publishes from SOURCE ONLY. Nothing produced on a developer machine, no editor or
# IDE state, and no version-control or CI metadata may enter the build context. That keeps the
# context a few kilobytes, keeps layer caching honest, and - most importantly - stops host build
# output from being copied in and poisoning the in-container restore, build, and publish.
#
# This is NOT .gitignore, and neither file substitutes for the other. The Docker-only entries
# below (.github/, Dockerfile, .dockerignore, README.md, LICENSE) are deliberately TRACKED in
# Git and must never be added to .gitignore; conversely .gitignore lists generated artifacts
# whose only overlap with this file is the build-output section.
#
# WARNING - never add a pattern that matches anything the Dockerfile copies into the build
# stage: the SDK pin, either Directory.*.props manifest, the root editor-config file that
# carries the path-scoped analyzer exemption, the .sln, src/, or tests/. The in-container build
# runs with code-style enforcement and warnings-as-errors, so silently dropping one of them
# surfaces as an opaque "file not found" or analyzer failure rather than an obvious mistake.
#
# Patterns are matched against the context root. The recursive **/ form is used wherever an
# artifact can occur at any depth (per-project bin/ and obj/ above all), and the plain form
# where the path only ever exists at the root.

## Build output - regenerated inside the SDK stage; must never leak in from the host
**/bin/
**/obj/
artifacts/
publish/
**/*.binlog

## Test and coverage output
**/TestResults/
**/*.trx
**/coverage*.*

## Version control and CI metadata (not needed to build the solution)
.git/
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github/

## Container definitions (inputs to `docker build` itself, not to the build inside it)
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
docker-compose*.yml

## IDE / editor state
.vs/
.vscode/
.idea/
**/*.user
**/*.suo
**/*.DotSettings.user

## Documentation (not an input to the build)
README.md
LICENSE

## OS noise - recursive form so a stray file is caught at any depth, root included
**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db
**/*~
